<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-Feb trade surplus widens to $4.6 bln.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-Feb trade surplus widens to $4.6 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $4.6 billion in the first two months of this year after a $3.0 billion surplus in the same period of 1996, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>Total trade, including other members of CIS</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Feb 97    Jan 97    Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>    exports			    13.2	   6.4	  n/a</p>
<p>    imports			     8.6	   3.7	  n/a</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +4.6	  +2.7	 +3.0</p>
<p>Excluding trade with other members of CIS</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Feb 97    Jan 97    Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>    exports			    10.4	   5.1	  n/a</p>
<p>    imports			     6.2	   2.6	  n/a</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +4.2	  +2.5	 +3.4</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
